  "changes": [
    "Rust ActionGraph owns the tools.history structural root, ordered history-row identities, parent edges and History typed payloads. Payloads retain UTF-16 title/detail/display URL; Rust defines the 60px row height. Localized date formatting and admitted profile/query/limit inputs remain native.",
    "The Rust/Metal result consumer reconciles actual native children by Rust node ID and live owner token. It reuses/reorders retained RustRowView adapters, creates only missing rows and removes stale/deleted rows. Retained rows skip RowButton::Spec, scene-visible callback and domain callback reconstruction. Views retains its existing rebuild path.",
    "Identical batches preserve leases, focus and pending input. Title/detail/display-URL changes cancel the affected row press; membership/order changes cancel all history presses. Surviving node IDs and parent edges remain stable. Explicit native canvas invalidation handles cancellation that already occurred inside Rust.",
    "The native history identity remains a framed profile/URL/exact-visit/duplicate-occurrence key. Callbacks on retained keys remain bound to the same native profile and GURL; no index target is captured or rewritten. Native posted navigation/profile validation and existing result admission remain unchanged. Query editing and full tools-form reconstruction still retire the scope.",
    "Graph and record owner tokens now permit O(1) checks that an input lease belongs to the expected graph. Numeric IDs alone are not sufficient across windows/scopes. Both workspace-switcher and history reuse consumers check ownership; replaced/retired/unbound handles reject ownership. Tokens retain identity safely without using reusable graph addresses.",
    "History projection updates native title/detail/height, URL tooltip/AX name and detail AX description from the Rust snapshot. The URL AX-name convention matches the existing Rust history-row adapter; this change does not establish AX parity with Views. Native View properties remain projections, and model/node borrows finish before callbacks.",
    "Twelve new Rust cases cover history tree properties/raw UTF-16, identical projection, content cancellation, order/membership, retirement/readmission, invalid/type admission, empty/query lifetime, parent/lease replacement, owned snapshots/graph drop and equal-ID foreign-scope rejection. Two new compiled-only browser cases cover retained native identity/focus/AX and reordered callback targets. The existing history replacement test now expects View reuse plus cancelled input. None of those browser cases was executed."
  ],
  "deferred_gui_cases": [
    "ZitterProfilesBrowserTest.HistorySceneReusesRowsAcrossPresentationOrderAndMembership",
    "ZitterProfilesBrowserTest.HistorySceneReorderCancelsPressAndKeepsNativeCallbackTarget",
