  ],
  "limits": [
    "No browser UI tests, physical input or manual acceptance were run, per instruction. Pure Rust tests and compilation do not prove native focus/AX/capture/scroll/reveal behavior or visual parity.",
    "Workspace-switcher and history-row subtrees now own real parent/properties/order and have incremental native consumers. Complete form/sidebar/palette trees, editor/text ownership and full window/container lifetime coordination remain open.",
    "Empty-state and status copy still come from the existing ToolsForm projection; the empty-state text adapter is recreated. Query edits and full tools-page rebuilds deliberately retire the history scene; values/adapters do not persist across those boundaries.",
    "History command authorization and formatting stay native. Rust scene keys and owner tokens only identify UI leases and do not authorize browser/profile operations. URL AX-name parity with Views and broader platform accessibility require the deferred checkpoint.",
    "Owner tokens add storage/reference-counting work; scene reconciliation and owned snapshots have unmeasured cost. No memory, CPU/GPU or actual-presentation speedup is claimed. No new third-party or target dependencies were added.",
    "The running preview was left unchanged. Full UI/manual checks, CPU/GPU/presentation profiling, compositor diagnostics and final release/license acceptance remain open. Frozen UI-lab bootstrap/network inputs exclude current-main network policy."
  ],
